 # Gaussian Avatars
 
-Also called: FLAME Gaussian Splatting, PSAvatar, PSAvatar / Relightable Avatar, Relightable Avatar
+Also called: FLAME Gaussian Splatting, PSAvatar, PSAvatar / Relightable Avatar, Relightable Avatar [S2, unofficial]
 
 ## Overview
-Gaussian Avatars is a method for reconstructing photorealistic, animatable head avatars by anchoring 3D Gaussians to a parametric FLAME mesh [S1][S3, unofficial]. It associates each FLAME mesh triangle with a Gaussian that is optimized for the scene while being constrained to remain within its corresponding triangle [S1][S3, unofficial]. Unlike methods that predict Gaussian parameters via feedforward networks conditioned on pose [S1], Gaussian Avatars optimizes the Gaussian ellipsoid parameters directly while enforcing geometric constraints, enabling high-fidelity rendering and relighting [S2, unofficial].
+Gaussian Avatars reconstructs photorealistic, animatable head avatars by anchoring 3D Gaussians to a parametric FLAME mesh [S1][S3, unofficial]. It associates each FLAME mesh triangle with a Gaussian that is optimized for the scene while being constrained to remain within its corresponding triangle [S1][S3, unofficial]. Unlike methods that predict Gaussian parameters via feedforward networks conditioned on pose [S1], Gaussian Avatars optimizes the Gaussian ellipsoid parameters directly while enforcing geometric constraints, enabling high-fidelity rendering and relighting [S2, unofficial].
 
